# suite-selection-map.data - Explicit map rows for a touched path `scripts/lib/suite-resolver-lib.sh`'s
# default-backend pre-pass (basename resolution via suite-selection-lib.sh) leaves unresolved.
# This is the "adding a row is the normal repair" surface deliverable 2(b) of the originating
# record names: when a real, covering suite exists for a path that basename pairing and the
# grep-based reference lookup both miss, add a row here rather than accepting the escalation to
# a classified fallback (NO-SUITE-BY-CLASS / OWED-NOT-PAID).
#
# Format: one row per path pattern, TAB-separated, 3 fields: path_glob  suites  reason
#   path_glob  A bash glob pattern (matched via `[[ "$path" == $path_glob ]]`, under which `*`
#              CROSSES `/` -- the same matching semantics `.claude-extensions.json`'s
#              `coupled_generated_surfaces.trigger_glob` already uses; see
#              context/standards/repo-level-declarations.md). Matched against the repo-relative
#              touched path exactly as given to the resolver.
#   suites     Comma-separated suite basename(s) this path pattern maps to (e.g.
#              "test-verify-touched.sh" or "test-verify-touched.sh,test-run-all-selection.sh").
#              Each basename must exist on disk -- the entry-point's own preflight
#              (scripts/verify-touched.sh) refuses to run with a named row whose suite does not
#              exist, before any suite runs.
#   reason     Free text: why basename resolution misses this path and why the named suite(s)
#              actually cover it. Never interpreted; diagnostic only.
#
# Rows are checked in file order; the FIRST matching row wins (no accumulation across rows for
# one path). A path matching no row here falls through to the Phase 3 classified fallback
# (NO-SUITE-BY-CLASS or OWED-NOT-PAID), never silently to nothing.
#
# This plan's own authoring already demonstrates the two classes of path basename resolution
# misses: a brand-new library/script under scripts/lib/ or scripts/ whose own test suite exists
# but is not yet discoverable by name pairing until the suite itself lands (self-referential at
# authoring time, resolved once the suite is committed), and a checked-in *.data file with no
# "test-" counterpart at all.
scripts/lib/verification-scope-lib.sh	test-verification-scope-lib.sh	new library; its own suite test-verification-scope-lib.sh is added in a later phase of the record that created it
scripts/lib/suite-resolver-lib.sh	test-suite-resolver-lib.sh	new library; its own suite test-suite-resolver-lib.sh is added in a later phase of the record that created it
scripts/lib/unmapped-fallback-lib.sh	test-unmapped-fallback-lib.sh	new library; its own suite test-unmapped-fallback-lib.sh is added in a later phase of the record that created it
scripts/verify-touched.sh	test-verify-touched.sh	new entry point; basename pairing alone would already find test-verify-touched.sh, this row documents the intent explicitly so the entry point never falls through to the classified fallback for its own source file
scripts/report-suite-coverage.sh	test-verify-touched.sh	coverage report is exercised by the same suite as the entry point it is published alongside; no dedicated suite exists for this reporter alone
scripts/tests/suite-selection-map.data	test-suite-resolver-lib.sh	checked-in data file with no "test-" counterpart basename; the resolver library's own suite covers its format and lookup behaviour
scripts/tests/suite-selection-noclass.data	test-unmapped-fallback-lib.sh	checked-in data file with no "test-" counterpart basename; the fallback classification library's own suite covers its format and lookup behaviour
